# Roster: cons/head/tail, put/get/remove, times

Arrays and maps are copied on write. Target can later name a persistent or mutating backing store; for now copy is fine.

`head` / `tail` pull an array apart. Empty head or tail fails at runtime.
`get` / `remove` take a map apart. A missing key fails at runtime.
`times` on Int runs a block with the index from 0.

## Schema

```
Team = String/name [Player]/players {String : Int}/scores
Player = String/name Int/score
```

## Construction

```
[:Team
  "Rockets"
  [:Array/Player
    ["Ada" 3]
    ["Cy" 5]
  ]
  {String:Int "Ada":3 "Cy":5}
]
```

## Methods

```
Player::tag = { name.concat(":").concat(score) }

Player::initial = { name.substring(0, 1) }

Team::headline = { name.concat(" x").concat(players.length()) }

Team::captain = { players.head() }

Team::bench = { players.tail() }

Team::adaScore = { scores.get("Ada") }

Team::noAda = { scores.remove("Ada") }

Team::addNamed = {n, s |
  p = [:Player n s].
  [:Team name players.cons(p) scores.put(n, s)]
}

Team::withDi = { this.addNamed("Di", 7) }

Team::fresh = { [:Team name [:Array/Player] {String:Int}] }

Team::zeros = { 13.times({ i | i*1 }) }
```

## Target

```
%terminal

%main
public static function main():Void {
    var team = TeamAssemblage.factory();
    var helper = new WCHNTHelper();
    trace(team.toConstruction(0, helper));
    trace("headline");
    trace(team.headline());
    trace("captain");
    trace(team.captain().toConstruction(0, helper));
    trace("bench");
    trace(helper.arrayToConstruction(team.bench(), 0));
    trace("adaScore");
    trace(team.adaScore());
    trace("noAda");
    trace(helper.mapToConstruction(team.noAda(), 0));
    trace("withDi");
    trace(team.withDi().toConstruction(0, helper));
    trace("fresh");
    trace(team.fresh().toConstruction(0, helper));
    trace("zeros");
    trace(helper.arrayToConstruction(team.zeros(), 0));
}
```
